# SEO rules for pages

Source of truth: `docs/SEO-PLAYBOOK.md` (sections 2, 3, 6), `docs/KEYWORD-MAP.md`. Enforced by `npm run audit:seo` and `npm run audit:page-checklist` (run `npm run build` first). Thresholds live in `scripts/audit/lib.mjs` `LIMITS`.

## Research first (before any new or reworked page)
- One primary query; name the intent (do / know / compare / navigate) and match the page type.
- Check the live top results and plan one gap (worked example, sourced formula, table, reverse mode).
- Check `docs/KEYWORD-MAP.md` for cannibalization; extend an existing page instead of cloning intent.
- List 3–6 PAA / secondary questions for H2s and FAQ.
- Full reusable checklist: keep the items in `uploads/page-checklist` spirit — keyword research, structure, metadata, schema, internal links, cited sources, mobile 390×844, performance, ship/verify.

## Keyword ownership
- One primary keyword per page, unique across the site. Register it in `docs/KEYWORD-MAP.md` **before** creating the page. A phrasing of an owned intent is a secondary keyword of the owner, never a new page.
- Primary keyword appears in: `<title>` (first), the H1, the first paragraph, the slug, the meta description. `keywords[0]` in `src/data/tools.ts` equals the keyword-map primary.
- Do not create per-breed, per-city, per-phrasing or per-food pages without unique, sourced data (scaled-content abuse). Use options on the one tool page.

## Head
- Title: <= **60** characters **including** the ` | PetCalc Tools` suffix added by `BaseLayout.astro` (hard max 60; `audit:seo-guardrails` fails over); unique; not stuffed.
- Meta description: **50-165** characters, unique, states what the user gets and "free"; no quotes that break the attribute.
- Exactly one `<h1>`; heading levels never skip; H2s are descriptive ("Worked example", "Formula and method").
- Canonical: exactly one, absolute `https`, self-referencing, built from `absoluteUrl()`; never `pages.dev`; query-string calculator state never changes it. Trailing slash always.
- Open Graph/Twitter complete (`og:title/description/url/type/image`); `og:image` is a raster file (PNG/JPG/WebP) 1200x630; `og:url` equals canonical.
- Do not add `noindex` to content pages. Only `/embed/*` and `/404` are noindex (embeds canonicalise to their tool).
- `<html lang>` and viewport required.

## Body / answer-first
- First paragraph is answer-first (`class="answer-first"` / guide `lead`), 40-60 words, with a **number or clear verdict** in sentence 1–2 where one exists.
- On tool pages the calculator sits above the fold on mobile (≤80 words before the first input; cookie bar ≤56px).
- On hubs/home: 1–2 sentence lead, then the **card grid** (first card well above the fold)—no long prose before the cards.
- Required sections for tools: how to use, formula/method (visible), worked example (numbers equal the unit test), assumptions/limits, FAQ (5–8), sources, related tools. Tools >= 600 words; guides >= 800 words.
- Cite every number/threshold to `src/data/sources.ts`; never invent reviewers, “vet-approved”, or `reviewedBy` schema without a real named reviewer.
- >= 2 contextual links to other tools/guides in the body; descriptive anchors (never "click here"); every internal href ends with `/`.
- No placeholder, lorem, “coming soon”, “— not a calculator page”, or internal KD notes in visible copy.

## Structured data
- Use the shells (`ToolPageShell` -> `WebApplication` price 0; `GuidePageShell` -> `Article` with `dateModified`, `citation` URLs) and `BaseLayout` (`Organization`, `WebSite`, `BreadcrumbList`). Hubs may add `CollectionPage` + `ItemList`.
- No `aggregateRating`/`review`/`HowTo`/`reviewedBy` unless real on-site data / a configured reviewer exists.

## Registries and routes
- Every page has a registry entry (`src/data/tools.ts` / `guides.ts`) with a unique `description` <= 160 chars; reciprocal `related` links; no registry entry without a page.
- Slug = primary keyword, lowercase, hyphenated, never changed after publish without 301s in `public/_redirects` **and** `vercel.json`.
- Sitemap is automatic (`@astrojs/sitemap`); new indexable pages must appear there, embeds/404 must not.
- Update `docs/KEYWORD-MAP.md` and `buildDate` with every new page (`llms.txt` is generated).

## Before you finish
Run `npm run audit` (includes `audit:page-checklist`). Zero errors required; warnings explained.
